{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. ___ . I'm Dr. ___ , your oncologist. You're here today for your 19th cycle of high-dose methotrexate as part of reinduction therapy for your CNS lymphoma. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:21:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Morning, Doctor. I’m feeling okay—no headaches, no nausea, and no seizures lately. Just a bit tired, but I expected that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:22:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. We’ll be starting your methotrexate infusion today around noon. You’ll also continue your temozolomide at home starting tonight, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:23:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I brought my pills with me. I take 140 mg and 100 mg each night. Should I take them later today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll give you the dose tonight before bed. We also need to start sodium bicarbonate to protect your kidneys during the chemo. You’ll get that through your IV."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:25:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Is the methotrexate going to make me feel worse than usual?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:26:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Some patients feel fatigue or mild nausea, but we’ll give you ondansetron if needed. Most tolerate it well, especially since you’ve had it before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:27:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s reassuring. And my desmopressin—I take it three times a day for my diabetes insipidus. Will I still get that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:28:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll continue your desmopressin nasal spray. But we’ll monitor your sodium closely because the IV fluids and desmopressin can sometimes lower it too much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember last time my sodium dropped. Was that why I felt so weak?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:30:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. We caught it early. This time, we’ll check your labs frequently and adjust fluids if needed. No need to worry unless it drops again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. And my seizure meds—levetiracetam—I’ve been taking them regularly. Should I skip any dose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:32:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, keep taking them as prescribed. We don’t want any breakthrough seizures. You said your last one was a few months ago?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I fell and lost consciousness. Scared me, but no injury. I’ve been careful since."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:34:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep you on full seizure prevention. Also, your blood pressure is stable—139 over 82. You’re still on lisinopril?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, 5 mg daily. No headaches or dizziness, so I think it’s working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:36:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll continue it. Any anxiety or trouble sleeping lately?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little anxious before chemo, but propranolol helps. I take trazodone at night if I can’t sleep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2186-06-16 09:38:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s fine. We’ll keep those available as needed. I’ll see you again after the infusion starts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2186-06-16 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting your methotrexate infusion now. It’ll take a few hours. The nurse will monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2186-06-16 12:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I feel it going in. No discomfort so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2186-06-17 06:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your methotrexate level came back at 205—right on track. We’ll keep up the IV fluids and sodium bicarbonate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2186-06-17 06:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that high? Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2186-06-17 06:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s expected this early. It’ll go down over the next few days. We’re watching it closely to make sure it clears properly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2186-06-17 06:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my sodium? I remember it dropped last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2186-06-17 06:10:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s 137 now—normal. But we’re being cautious. We may reduce IV fluids later to prevent it from dropping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2186-06-17 06:11:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I appreciate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2186-06-18 05:58:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your labs are back. Your methotrexate level is down to 0.08—that’s excellent. But your sodium is now 127."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2186-06-18 05:59:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s low again. Should I stop my desmopressin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2186-06-18 06:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll hold it for now and reduce your IV fluids. We’ll also give you some IV sodium chloride to bring it up safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2186-06-18 06:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that affect my diabetes insipidus symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2186-06-18 06:03:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly—you might feel more thirsty or urinate more. But it’s temporary. We’ll restart desmopressin once your sodium is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2186-06-18 06:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can handle that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2186-06-18 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your sodium is improving—now at 129. We’ll keep monitoring it. You’re doing well overall."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2186-06-18 10:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2186-06-18 10:32:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If your labs stay stable, likely tomorrow morning. We’ll check one more set of labs tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2186-06-18 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my next treatment? When is that scheduled?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2186-06-18 10:35:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "In about two weeks. Your oncology team will contact you to arrange it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2186-06-18 10:36:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need to take anything special before the next dose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2186-06-18 10:37:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, just like this time—sodium bicarbonate the day before to protect your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2186-06-19 05:58:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your sodium is 127, stable, and your methotrexate level is 0.08. You’re cleared for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Do I restart my desmopressin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:01:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, go back to your usual three times daily. Keep an eye on your thirst and urination."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds—everything else stays the same?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:03:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, all your home medications continue as before—lisinopril, sertraline, levetiracetam, and temozolomide."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about signs I should watch for? When to call?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call if you develop fevers, chills, numbness, dizziness, or any seizure-like activity. Also, if you feel unusually weak or confused."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:07:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll follow up with your neuro-oncologist. They’ll contact you to schedule it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:10:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:11:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You did well this round. Rest up, and we’ll see you in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:12:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will bring your discharge papers and prescriptions shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:15:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:16:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. ___. Stay hydrated and keep up with your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:17:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:20:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor your progress. Let us know if anything comes up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:22:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. I’m grateful for the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re part of the team. We’re glad you’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:25:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, Doctor. I’ll see you next time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:26:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:27:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will assist you with discharge soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:30:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2186-06-19 06:31:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2186-06-16 09:20:00",
    "admission_end": "2186-06-19 11:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 65-year-old man with recurrent CNS lymphoma was admitted for his 19th cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy as part of reinduction therapy. He presented in stable condition with no acute symptoms and tolerated the infusion well. His hospital course was complicated by mild hyponatremia (sodium 127), managed with fluid restriction and temporary adjustment of desmopressin. Methotrexate levels declined appropriately to 0.08 by discharge. He remained neurologically stable, seizure-free, and hemodynamically normal. He was discharged home on his full regimen of home medications with follow-up scheduled in two weeks.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Other malignant lymphomas, lymph nodes of head, face, and neck",
      "Diabetes insipidus",
      "Hyposmolality and/or hyponatremia",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, without mention of intractable epilepsy",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Adjustment disorder with mixed anxiety and depressed mood"
    ]
  }
}
